title: Defence Droids for the Trade Federation
subtitle: The guilds want private armies to fight the pirates.
tags: event
view-if: date >= 6
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
face-image: img/ev_trade.svg

= Defence Droids for the Trade Federation

The Trade Federation has asked the Commerce Committee for permission to expand its "defensive" droid forces, citing the plague of piracy on the Rim. The committee, chaired by a guild ally, seems certain to agree. Several Caucus senators point out that a private army big enough to fight pirates is big enough to fight planets.

- @fight: Fight it in committee.
- @inspect: Allow it, but demand Judicial inspections of the droid foundries.
- @accept: Accept it as a reasonable answer to piracy.

@fight
subtitle: −1 political capital. The guilds will not forget.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough political capital.
on-arrival: capital -= 1; guild_relation -= 8; tf_droids_limited = 1; hawk_dissent -= 3; rc_momentum += 0.5

The Caucus forces the request into a long, embarrassing public hearing. The final authorisation is a fraction of what the Federation wanted. Someone at the Federation's headquarters on Neimoidia is said to have broken a desk.

@inspect
subtitle: The droids will be built, but we will know where.
on-arrival: guild_relation -= 3; tf_inspections = 1; judicial_forces += 0.2

The Federation agrees to inspections through gritted teeth. The Judicial Department's first report runs to nine hundred pages. Somewhere on page six hundred is a supplier on Geonosis.

@accept
subtitle: The guilds will be grateful; the Rim may be safer.
on-arrival: guild_relation += 6; rim_hardship -= 1; tf_droids = 1; rimward_dissent += 3; hawk_dissent += 4

The authorisation passes without debate. Federation battleships soon patrol the Rim's trade lanes, and the pirates retreat. The Hawks mutter that the Caucus has just paid for someone else's army.
